Sandra met [[Eathon Lambert]] and the pair eventually married and had two children, [[Kathy Lambert|Kathy]] and [[Lok]]. Eathon once took Sandra for a picnic in the valley of [[Tír na nÓg]] to which she gave him a smack as he had promised he'd retired from adventuring. {{source|Back Home}} After Eathon disappeared, Sandra was left to raise her children on her own. {{source|Home Turf}}

The Huntik team stayed with Sandra at the [[Lambert house]] while on vacation. Sandra spoke to Dante about how she missed Eathon and how she couldn't bear to lose Lok too. After the team traveled to [[Newgrange Passage Tomb]] with [[Scarlet Byrne]], Sandra came to Lok's rescue and helped defeat [[Klaus]]' [[Suits]]. {{source|Home Turf}}

Lok revealed to [[Cherit]] in the [[Tomb of Nefertiti]] that Sandra had got him a bird when he was six, contrary to the bicycle, baseball bat and toy he had wanted. This became key to solving the puzzle and recovering [[Eathon Lambert's puzzle]]. {{source|The Sceptre Deception}}

The team stayed as Sandra's again after being defeated by [[Rassimov]] in [[Egypt]]. {{source|Back Home}}

During the final battle, Sandra secretly joined Scarlet as a co-pilot on a [[Scramjet]] despite being retired. {{source|The Spiral Mark}} She was shocked to hear of Dante's death and joined the battle against the [[Blood Spiral]]. {{source|Lok and the Betrayer}} During the final battle against [[The Betrayer]], Sandra fought alongside [[Lucas Casterwill]] but both were paralyzed by the Betrayer's [[Shadowlock]] power. After his defeat, Sandra was freed and celebrated the triumph. {{source|Dante's Return}}

